@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Patch 0073: smoother transitions on most pages (new Training list, 1 of 7)
+
+Stacks on 0072. Your new list of seven corrections is numbered **0073 to 0079**, one patch each, in your order: 1 page transitions, 2 animated Guide, 3 off-course handling in the Checks, 4 themed highlight, 5 smoother stage and step changes, 6 hint feedback, 7 virtual terminal. (The first list, Info style, sharp Show, cropped text and one-screen Show, was already done in 0066 to 0070 and 0071.)
+
+## What you asked for
+- Smoother transitions on most pages.
+
+## Where 0071 stopped
+0071 made Training pages (and the cart and Pay while a course runs) slide, and said the rest was "one line". Everything else still cut: pages, tabs and the guided checkout's steps.
+
+## Fix
+1. **Every pushed page slides in** (`isAnimatedRoute` is now true for any named page). Forward arrives from the right, back from the left, anything else rises. Unchanged: Reduce Motion turns it off.
+2. **The old page leaves too, only where that is safe** (`canLeaveDrawn`, `LEAVE_DRAWN` in `src/lib/motion.ts`). The leaving page is drawn again as a fresh copy, so it has to look right from stored data alone. Lists and read-only screens (Saved carts, Orders, Items, Customers, Reports, Gift cards, Drawer, Settings, Staff, Diagnostics, Help, Training, the cart) leave smoothly. **Pay, Create item and Edit item never do**: Pay depends on a sale in flight and the item forms on unsaved text, so redrawing them would flash blank or wrong content. They simply give way to the page that arrives, which still slides in.
+3. **Tabs fade and rise** when you switch (`Enter` keyed by tab for Inventory, Transactions, Notifications and More; `TabPane` for Checkout). Checkout is not remounted, so the cart and scanner state survive exactly as before; `TabPane` only replays the animation when the tab becomes active.
+4. **Guided checkout steps fade and rise** (Customer, Discount, Review, Pay each wrapped in `Enter`; the item picker uses `TabPane` because it stays mounted so the grid keeps its place).
+
+## Tests
+- `tests/motion.test.ts`: every named page animates, a change needs only one side, which pages may be redrawn while leaving (and that Pay and the item forms may not, unless a course is running), and the tab fade is shorter than the page slide.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] `motion.ts`: `LEAVE_DRAWN`, `canLeaveDrawn`, `isAnimatedRoute` for every page, `TAB_ENTER_MS`.
+2. [x] `RouteTransition.tsx` keeps the old page only when `canLeaveDrawn`.
+3. [x] `Motion.tsx` `TabPane`; `App.tsx` uses it and `Enter` for the tabs.
+4. [x] `GuidedCheckout.tsx` steps wrapped.
+5. [ ] You: on the iPad, open Settings, Orders, Reports and come back; switch every tab; take a card payment (Pay should slide in and then give way, never flash blank); in a Simple or Minimal staff mode step through the guided checkout. Tell me anything that flashes, feels too slow (a slide is 380 ms, a tab fade 280 ms) or fights the scanner.
+6. [ ] You: if a page you use a lot looks wrong while it leaves, tell me its name and I will take it off `LEAVE_DRAWN`.
